{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אך אם יום", :translit "akh im yom", :gloss "but if a day"} {:he "מעת לעת", :translit "me'et la'et", :gloss "from time to time"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins with alef (אך) and ends with alef (יום), teaching that the victim must survive twenty-four hours"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'מעת לעת' denotes a full twenty-four-hour period. In the context of Exodus 21:21, if the beaten slave survives 'a day or two days' before dying, the master is not liable for murder. The Talmud applies this to mean the victim must live a full twenty-four hours from the blow (Rashi on Exodus 21:21 citing Sanhedrin).", :sources ["Rashi on Exodus 21:21" "Sanhedrin 78b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יוקם", :translit "yukam", :gloss "he shall be avenged / he shall stand"} {:he "יוקם קין", :translit "yukam kayin", :gloss "Cain shall be avenged"} {:he "כל הורג קין שבעתים יוקם", :translit "kol horeg kayin shiv'atayim yukam", :gloss "all who kill Cain sevenfold shall be avenged"} {:he "לא יוקם כי כספו הוא", :translit "lo yukam ki kaspoh hu", :gloss "he shall not be avenged for he is his money"} {:he "קניתי איש את ה'", :translit "kaniti ish et Hashem", :gloss "I have acquired a man with HaShem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["יוקם" "יוקם קין" "יקם"]}], :frame {:text "The word 'יוקם' links Exodus 21:21 to the two occurrences in Genesis 4:15 and 4:24. Rabbi Meir rules that if one sells his slave for thirty days, the first buyer is judged for 'a day or two days' but not the second, since acquisition of produce-rights (פירות) is not equivalent to acquisition of the body (גוף) — and 'כי כספו הוא' applies only when the body itself is owned, not merely its labor. The verse 'קניתי איש את ה'׳' (Genesis 4:1) demonstrates that 'קנין' denotes full bodily ownership.", :sources ["Gittin 40a" "Genesis 4:1" "Genesis 4:15" "Genesis 4:24" "Exodus 21:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כספו", :translit "kaspoh", :gloss "his money"} {:he "כדין לכהמה", :translit "kadin likhemah", :gloss "judgment for an animal"} {:he "מעת לעת", :translit "me'et la'et", :gloss "from time to time"} {:he "ריסוק אברים", :translit "risuk evarim", :gloss "crushing of limbs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "כספו", :b "כדין לכהמה"}], :frame {:text "The law of 'מעת לעת' — requiring the injured party to survive a full twenty-four hours for murder liability — applies also to animals in cases of crushing limbs, as derived in Sanhedrin 78b. The gematria of 'כספו' equating to 'כדין לכהמה' signals that the same twenty-four-hour standard governs both human and animal cases of bodily injury.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 78b" "Bava Kamma 26b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse begins with alef (אך) and ends with alef (יום), teaching that the victim must survive twenty-four hours", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["יוקם" "יוקם קין" "יקם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "יוקם", :refs ["Genesis 4:8" "Genesis 4:15" "Genesis 4:24" "Genesis 13:17" "Genesis 18:16" "Genesis 19:1" "Genesis 19:14" "Genesis 19:15"], :n 380, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "יוקם קין", :refs ["Genesis 4:8" "Genesis 4:24"], :n 2, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "יקם", :refs ["Genesis 4:15" "Genesis 4:24" "Genesis 27:31" "Exodus 21:21" "Joshua 10:13" "1 Samuel 1:23" "Jeremiah 28:6" "Psalms 107:29"], :n 8, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "כספו", :a-value 166, :b "כדין לכהמה", :b-value 184, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:15.995068432Z", :model "glm-5.2"}